# Router Advertisement of a typical home router (ICMPv6 type 134, RFC 4861 section 4.2): M and
# O both off, SLAAC only. The router is fe80::200:5eff:fe00:5301 (documentation MAC
# 00:00:5e:00:53:01); the message is the ICMPv6 payload, without the IPv6 header. The checksum
# is as a capture shows it; the parser does not verify it (the kernel does on a raw socket).
#
# type 134, code 0, checksum 0x1a2b
86 00 1a 2b
# cur hop limit 64, flags 0x00 (M off, O off, preference medium), router lifetime 1800 s
40 00 07 08
# reachable time 0, retransmit timer 0 (unspecified)
00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00
# option 1, source link-layer address, 1 unit of 8 octets: 00:00:5e:00:53:01
01 01 00 00 5e 00 53 01
# option 5, MTU, 1 unit: reserved 0, MTU 1500
05 01 00 00 00 00 05 dc
# option 3, prefix information, 4 units: prefix length 64, flags 0xc0 (L, A)
03 04 40 c0
# valid lifetime 86400 s, preferred lifetime 14400 s, reserved
00 01 51 80
00 00 38 40
00 00 00 00
# prefix 2001:db8:100::
20 01 0d b8 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
